{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIwL0hlcm9lcyUyMCUyODIwMjAlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Heroes","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/9LLR6EESbxDILndkyUkciEPuRyI.jpg","description":"Displaying the faces and voices of transgender youth, the documentary short shows the authenticity of queer and trans people living in Toronto, while simultaneously discussing the struggles for self-acceptance that people who do not conform to cisgender and heteronormative ideals of gender face. Andy Nguyen, trans director and film student, captures his trans friends in their natural state on 16mm film shot on a Bolex h16 camera. Accompanied by narration written and recited by Salem Rao, this film represents that trans people exist and this is what we look like. Regardless of the obvious everyday transphobia, trans people find community and uniqueness within each other and themselves.\n\nReleased 11 Nov 2020 · Canada · Language: English · 2 min\nStudio: andyvisualz, Toronto Metropolitan University\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2020","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"10.0","runtime":"2 min","cast":["Salem Rao","Adrian Bifolchi","Jo Scott","Kai Kuelz","Kai Grenier","Mikhael Klassen-Kay","Nicholas Ginther","Minh Tam Huynh"],"director":["Trâm Anh Nguyễn"],"released":"2020-11-11T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"A documentation of the faces and voices of trans youth in Toronto.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Trâm Anh Nguyễn","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/fZuCUKilDAmHi57eST69V0wZ4T4.jpg"},{"name":"Salem Rao","character":"Narrator & Himself"},{"name":"Adrian Bifolchi","character":"Himself"},{"name":"Jo Scott","character":"Themself"},{"name":"Kai Kuelz","character":"Himself"},{"name":"Kai Grenier","character":"Himself"},{"name":"Mikhael Klassen-Kay","character":"Himself"},{"name":"Nicholas Ginther","character":"Themself"},{"name":"Minh Tam Huynh","chara